Author: <a href="https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/profile.php?mode=viewprofile&u=35585" target="_blank">AS_Games</a><br />
	Posted: Wed Nov 18, 2026 5:51 pm (GMT 0)<br /><br /><span class="postbody">
	<blockquote>  <div class="attribution">Maxim wrote    <script type="text/javascript" src="./templates/select_expand_bbcodes.js"></script>    <script type="text/javascript">    
<!--
        var id = 'SXBB' + (1000 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000));        SXBB[id] = new _SXBB(id);        SXBB[id].T['select'] = 'Select';        SXBB[id].T['expand'] = '[+]';        SXBB[id].T['contract'] = '[-]';        SXBB[id].writeCmd();    
//-->
    </script>  </div>  <div class="body">    <script type="text/javascript">      
<!--
        SXBB[id].writeDiv();      
//-->
    </script>Let’s reserve judgment on the game until we can play it. There’s a range of opinions here and the only wrong attitude is to say someone else’s is wrong. LLMs are a tool, but that doesn’t make using them or not using them a superior position. But for the foreseeable future, we are segregating homebrew/ports where any content was generated by an LLM from those without, to help people easily filter on that axis.    <script type="text/javascript">      
<!--
        document.write('</div>');      
//-->
    </script>  </div></blockquote>
<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;What struck me here is that not a single person praised the initiative or the effort behind it—not even one line of feedback or appreciation for the game's artwork. Despite the graphics being hand-crafted by a Brazilian artist, the very first reaction was to ask if it was AI. It's a real shame, but we're living in a different era now, and things are going to change. I will finish this game. I'm Brazilian, and soon I'll be releasing it to the world.&quot;</span><br />

